# .env.example (COMMITTED template; the real srcs/.env is git-ignored)   READ: docs/04, 05
#
# PURPOSE
#   Subject: "it is mandatory to use a .env file to store environment variables".
#   Holds NON-SECRET configuration only. Passwords go to secrets/*.txt.
#   `make secrets` copies this file to srcs/.env if it doesn't exist.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around '=', no `export`.
#   Compose uses these for ${VAR} interpolation in docker-compose.yml.
#
# WRITE (suggested variables; rename freely, but keep them consistent everywhere)
#   LOGIN=alcacere
#   DOMAIN_NAME=alcacere.42.fr
#   DATA_PATH=/home/alcacere/data
#
#   # MariaDB
#   MYSQL_DATABASE=...            MYSQL_USER=...
#
#   # WordPress
#   WP_TITLE=...                  WP_URL=https://alcacere.42.fr
#   WP_ADMIN_USER=...  ☠ must NOT contain admin/Admin/administrator
#   WP_ADMIN_EMAIL=...
#   WP_USER=...                   WP_USER_EMAIL=...       WP_USER_ROLE=author
#
#   # TLS certificate subject
#   CERT_COUNTRY=ES  CERT_STATE=...  CERT_CITY=...  CERT_ORG=42  CERT_UNIT=student
#
#   # Bonus
#   REDIS_HOST=redis  REDIS_PORT=6379
#   FTP_USER=...      FTP_PASV_MIN=21000  FTP_PASV_MAX=21010  FTP_PASV_ADDRESS=...
#   PROMETHEUS_RETENTION=7d
#
# ☠ NO passwords in this file (it's committed).
